# Tracked paths deliberately left out of the scope map (#500).
#
# One `<glob>  # <reason>` per line, same glob dialect as .github/labeler.yml.
# The reason is not decoration: `.github/scope-coverage.py` refuses an entry
# without one, refuses one that has stopped matching any tracked path, and
# refuses one a scope row already covers. An exception here stays true or it
# goes red — the point is that the check is never silenced wholesale.
#
# Prefer a mapping. This list is for a path no scope OWNS, not for one whose
# owner is merely inconvenient to decide.

.gitignore  # Repository furniture: it governs the working tree for every scope at once and is the deliverable of none, so a mapping to any one scope would mislabel the next change made for another. Deliberately not an inventory of its entries — that list changes with every scope that adds a producer, and a reason that has to be re-read to stay true is a reason that quietly stops being one.
